    "rich_text_PBdNHL": {
      "type": "rich-text",
      "blocks": {
        "text_QATCky": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<h2>Advantages of working with NADCO</h2><ul><li><strong>Superior custom capabilities:</strong> We handle our designs in-house, working directly with clients to develop custom solutions that match their specifications</li><li><strong>Reduced lead times:</strong> Our full-service manufacturing line ensures that we don’t lose time waiting on parts from other facilities, creating efficient production processes and boosting our accountability</li><li><strong>Consistent quality and service:</strong> NADCO’s custom-designed products guarantee that nothing gets lost in translation between vendors, allowing us to maintain the same level of quality and service every time you work with us</li></ul><p></p><h3>Pressure Sensitive Labels</h3><p>Pressure sensitive labels are custom labels with an adhesive that responds to pressure without the need to apply water or other solvents. Workers can apply pressure sensitive labels to any surface with little effort, making them well suited for a broad range of consumer products.</p><p>Although end users only see the printed layer, pressure-sensitive labels actually consist of many layers, with each layer serving a specific purpose in the manufacturing process. Pressure-sensitive labels include a face-stock or printed layer, the adhesive layer, and a liner. The liner includes a release coating, which allows workers to remove the face stock and adhesive and apply the label to the product.</p><h2>How to Make Pressure-Sensitive Labels </h2><p>Some of the most common materials used in designing pressure-sensitive labels include:</p><ul><li><a href=\"/pages/foil-tape\" title=\"Foil Tape\"><strong>Foil</strong></a><strong>:</strong> Foil’s strength and versatility render it ideal for seaming, masking, and sealing tapes. Foil tapes resist weather, bend easily, and conform to irregular or uneven surfaces.</li><li><strong>Mylar:</strong> Mylar bonds well with a variety of challenging surfaces, creating adhesion that lasts for the product’s lifetime. Mylar consists of bright brushed silver polyester and has excellent dimensional stability, consistent surface smoothness, and endurance to varying temperatures.</li><li><strong>Vinyl:</strong> Perfect for labeling or striping, vinyl resists heat, bacteria, and corrosives, and it meets OSHA requirements. It can include ink-receptive coating and write-on capabilities.</li><li><strong>Paper subhead:</strong> Paper meets the widest variety of industrial applications. Paper tapes come in numerous forms, allowing you to customize its printability, tensile strength, removability, and more.</li></ul><h2>Advantages of Pressure Sensitive Adhesive Labels</h2><p>Pressure sensitive adhesive labels use thinner, lighter materials and form bonds with a wide range of surfaces, reducing assembly time for your final product. They provide uniform thickness and gap-filling characteristics while also insulating against noise and vibration. Using pressure sensitive labels also eliminates the need for mechanical fastenings or surface refinishing.</p><h3>What are the Advantages of Pressure-Sensitive Labels?</h3><p>Pressure-sensitive labels also have some product-specific advantages that include:</p><ul><li><strong>Convenience:</strong> Pressure sensitive labels can be removed from the liner and applied directly to the product without the addition of water or other solvents</li><li><strong>Variety:</strong> The wide range of customization options for pressure-sensitive labels ensures that you can find <a href=\"https://shopnadco.com/collections/labels\" title=\"https://shopnadco.com/collections/labels\">custom labels</a> for any need</li><li><strong>Adaptability:</strong> Pressure sensitive labels’ malleability means that you can adapt them to a variety of applications</li><li><strong>Efficiency:</strong> Due to their simplicity, pressure sensitive labels can be mass produced with ease, providing cost-effective and efficient labeling outcomes</li></ul><h2>Stick with NADCO for Your Adhesive Needs!</h2><p>NADCO provides high-quality, pressure sensitive tapes and labels along with additional full-service graphic designing, digital printing, die cutting, prototyping, and more.</p><p>We’re eager to help design your next custom printed tape or label. <a href=\"/pages/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"Contact us\">Contact us</a> directly or <a href=\"/pages/request-a-quote\" title=\"Request a Quote\">request a quote</a> today! </p>",
            "text_size": "text-inherit",
            "text_line_limit": "none",
            "button_style": "btn--underline",
            "button_icon": "none"
          }
        }
